-- EXCEPTIONS FROM ANOTHER LANGUAGE ----------------------------- main.kl  K0908

`try`, `catch`, `throw` and `raise` aren't Kalam keywords. Expected errors are values of type `Result`, so every function that can fail says so in its type.

10│     try:
        ^^^

Help: To fail, write `return Err(…)`. To pass a call's error up to your caller, put `?` after the call. To handle it, use `match` on the result.

Learn more: kalam explain K0908
